# PeaLang 0.31.0

PeaLang is an embeddable extension language with optional types, semantic analysis, PEAC bytecode/VM execution, sync and async embedding, FastAPI/Java/TypeScript/React integration, package management, observability, and signed package foundations.

## Signed package workflow

```bash
pea keygen publisher.key
pea build
pea sign my-package-1.0.0.peapkg publisher.key
pea verify my-package-1.0.0.peapkg my-package-1.0.0.peapkg.sig publisher.key
```

Version 0.31 adds SHA-256-bound HMAC signatures, trusted key storage, HTTPS registry policy, secure archive extraction, dependency-confusion safeguards, and installation receipts.

## Important security boundary

HMAC-SHA256 uses a shared signing secret. It is appropriate for controlled/internal distribution but not the final public-registry PKI. Public-key Ed25519 signing is the next package-security milestone.

